---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../config';
const updated = 'July 25, 2026';
---
<Base title="Terms of Service | Balance Bridge Financial" description="Terms governing use of the Balance Bridge Financial website and client portal.">
  <section class="bg-navy py-14"><div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold text-white">Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[14px] text-steel-400">Last updated: {updated}</p>
  </div></section>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12">
    <div class="prose-bb">
      <p>These terms govern your use of {BUSINESS.url} and the client portal at {BUSINESS.portalUrl}, operated by {BUSINESS.legalName}. By using the sites you agree to them. Client engagements are governed by a separate signed engagement letter; if these terms conflict with your engagement letter, the engagement letter wins. <!-- PLACEHOLDER: attorney review --></p>

      <h2>Website content is not professional advice</h2>
      <p>Articles, guides, checklists, and calculators on this site are general information for Texas small businesses — not accounting, tax, or legal advice for your specific situation, and reading them does not create a client relationship. Tax rules change; verify current figures with the relevant authority or a licensed professional. We coordinate tax preparation with clients' CPAs; we are not a CPA firm and do not provide attest services.</p>

      <h2>Client portal</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Portal accounts are created by invitation for active clients. You are responsible for keeping your credentials confidential and for activity under your account; enable multi-factor authentication.</li>
        <li>Upload only files relevant to your engagement and that you have the right to share. Don't upload malicious code or attempt to access other clients' data.</li>
        <li>E-signatures collected through the portal are intended to comply with the federal ESIGN Act and Texas UETA and are binding.</li>
        <li>We may suspend access to protect security or upon termination of an engagement; you may request an export of your documents.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Payments</h2>
      <p>Invoices are payable per your engagement letter. Card and bank payments are processed by Stripe; we don't store your full payment credentials.</p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>The site, brand, and content are ours or licensed to us. You may share links and brief quotes with attribution; don't republish substantial portions commercially without permission.</p>

      <h2>Disclaimers & liability</h2>
      <p>The websites are provided "as is." To the maximum extent permitted by law, we disclaim implied warranties for the websites and are not liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from website use. Nothing here limits liability that cannot be limited by law, or the terms of a signed engagement letter.</p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Texas. Venue for disputes about the websites lies in Texas courts. <!-- PLACEHOLDER: confirm county/venue --></p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions: {BUSINESS.email}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
